    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. it's a bit generic though. can you make it sound a little more warm and personal? like, maybe mention how hard the decision was for the team specifically, but keep it sounding like a professional tech company.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Let me try to infuse it with a bit more warmth and personality, while still maintaining a professional tone. Here's a revised sample email:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior Developer position at [Company Name]. We were blown away by your technical expertise and passion for innovation, and we were thrilled to have you join us for the final round of interviews.\n\nI want to start by saying how much we appreciated the time you took to speak with us, and how impressed we were by your insights on our company's technology stack. Your enthusiasm for our products and services was evident throughout the process, and we were grateful for the opportunity to learn more about your experiences and perspectives.\n\nHowever, after careful consideration, we've decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience align more closely with our current project needs. Please know that this decision was not made lightly, and it was an incredibly difficult choice for our team. We were all impressed by your qualifications, and we're sad to see you go.\n\nWe want to assure you that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as a developer. You have a unique set of skills that would be a valuable asset to any team",
      "source": "target",
